            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "include/dbus_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 93,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We have an existing variant type that is shared to reduce template bloat.  Please use it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/dbus_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 100,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please keep command-specific structures in command specific places.  This is for shared methods that have general usage."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/dbus_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 229,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "In general please don't create APIs that accept a dict for \"options\".  Enumerate your arguments using appropriate types.  If certain arguments are optional, use std::optional to declare that.\n\nIf the number of arguments gets too large (as we're getting close to the recommended cppcoreguidelines limit of 7 here) roll things into appropriate structs that can be passed as arguments."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/ipmi_https.hpp",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please use sendEx for new code, and implement flow control appropriately (wait for a write to finish before reading new data).\n\nNot doing that would be a potential dos/oom attack"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/ipmi_https.hpp",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This is going to invoke a data copy for every byte.  Is there a better api we can make for sendBinary that avoids that?  (one that accepts a span of bytes)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/ipmi_https.hpp",
                    "line": 80,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This is something we'll need to chat through with Vernon.  I'm not sure this will work as specified.  Can we start with an Admin-only impleemntation for simplification, and add roles as a followup?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/ipmi_https.hpp",
                    "line": 89,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please don't create static maps like this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/ipmi_https.hpp",
                    "line": 89,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "ok, i see this map is used later on in the method.  Please just encapsulate that full flow in a method with types as args."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/ipmi_https.hpp",
                    "line": 111,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Unsafe capture of conn.  If the connection is closed while the dbus request is happening, this will seg-fault."
                },
